    <task workspace="4cm" xml:id="act-changing-composite-crickets-celcius-task-3">
      <statement>
        <p>
						What is the domain of the function <m>H = G \circ D</m>?  What is its range?
					</p>
      </statement>
      <hint/>
      <answer><p>The domain of <m>H</m> is <m>[40, 180]</m> and the range is approximately <m>[10, 29.4]</m>.</p></answer>
      <solution>
        <p>
          As an abstract mathematical function, both the domain and range are all real
          numbers.  In the context of Dolbear's model (domain <m>[40, 180]</m> chirps per
          minute), the domain of <m>H</m> is <m>[40, 180]</m> and the corresponding range
          is approximately <m>[10, 29.4]</m> degrees Celsius.
        </p>
      </solution>
